CHAPTER.VERS:
The second admonition: what faults pastors (whom he referred to before under the word elders) ought to be void of, and what virtues they ought to have. For a bishop must be blameless, as the
Whom the Lord has appointed steward of his gifts. steward of God; not
Not stubborn and hard to please. selfwilled, not soon angry, not given to wine, no striker, not given to filthy lucre;

But a lover of hospitality, a lover of good men, 

          Cautious, and of a sound judgment, and of a singular example of moderation.
         sober, just, holy, temperate;

This witness is true. Wherefore rebuke them 

          Clearly and plainly, and do not go about the bush with them.
         sharply, that they may be sound in the faith;
